/**
 * The fixed data of the Brotli format (RFC 7932, Appendices A to C): the static dictionary of 122,784 bytes (stored deflated, as base64,
 * and unpacked once when it is first needed), the 121 word transforms, and the context lookup tables (2048 bytes). They are part of the
 * format, the same in every decoder; nothing here is chosen by canvast.
 */
export const DICTIONARY_DEFLATED = "";

/** The context lookup tables of the four context modes: 512 bytes each (the first 256 for the previous byte, the next 256 for the one before it). */
export const CONTEXT_LOOKUP = "";

/** The word transforms: a prefix, what is done to the word (0 as it is, 1 to 9 leave off that many letters at its end, 10 capitalise the first letter, 11 capitalise all, 12 to 20 leave off 1 to 9 at its start), a suffix. Prefixes and suffixes are bytes (UTF-8 spelled out as Latin 1). */
